- Story & Context: Parked on an abandoned siding in the pine marshes outside Kostomuksha, Ilya openly wept into a pocket tape recorder while running a dying battery synth through an infinite orbital-decay reverb tank. The conductor had discovered his unauthorized propagation bench wedged onto the carriage's high-voltage roof linkage, where tender rootlets were already frying into sticky, fragrant charcoal against the overhead wires. Leaning into the microphone with the bassoon weeping beneath him like a dying whale, Ilya muttered his confession to the insomniacs sitting in the dark berths: "I traded daylight for a root that never sleeps."
