Track 3: Etiolation Under Sodium Tubes
- Story & Context: The legendary run of Railcar 404 ended at the Black Ridge Trestle, where locals swear the train simply dissolved into an immovable, moss-draped monument beneath the sputtering amber station lights. Condensation ran down the double-paned glass like thick botanical sap as four insomniac bassoonists and a dozen passengers with tiny synth boards held a continuous four-hour drone, permanently locking the steel bogies to the tracks with tectonic sound pressure. By the time maintenance crews forced the hatch, the cabin was an unbreathable greenhouse jungle vibrating with residual sub-bass, its walls carved with the track's final lyric: "No morning can prise this iron from the moss."
